1
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:11,270
Hey.

2
00:00:12,110 --> 00:00:14,270
You're a cop, and you still watch crime films?

3
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,320
Don't you get bored?

4
00:00:15,510 --> 00:00:17,070
This takes me back to my childhood.

5
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:21,350
My grandma didn't have time to take me out much,

6
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:24,030
so she often took me to the cinema instead.

7
00:00:25,070 --> 00:00:26,960
We mostly watched crime films.

8
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,960
Did all those crime films make you

9
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:32,030
want to become a cop?

10
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:35,840
You could say that.

11
00:00:36,670 --> 00:00:39,840
When I was little, I thought all the leads looked so cool,

12
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:41,670
so when I grew up, I wanted to be a police officer

13
00:00:42,670 --> 00:00:45,390
to protect people and keep the peace.

14
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:46,470
It felt meaningful.

15
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:52,280
What are you doing?

16
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:55,280
Copying Tony Leung and tapping out Morse code?

17
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:57,880
Do you know what I just said?

18
00:00:58,320 --> 00:00:59,240
What did you say?

19
00:01:00,430 --> 00:01:01,430
Want to know?

20
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:03,150
Then learn it yourself.

21
00:01:04,870 --> 00:01:05,950
I'm not interested.

22
00:01:09,430 --> 00:01:11,640
Can't you show a little curiosity?

23
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:13,870
What if I only use Morse code from now on

24
00:01:13,870 --> 00:01:14,710
when I message you?

25
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:16,120
Go ahead.

26
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:18,710
If I can't understand it, I won't reply.

27
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:22,480
Go ahead and try. I dare you.

28
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:24,120
Stop messing around.

29
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:25,920
Watch the film.

30
00:01:27,230 --> 00:01:28,870
I still have to go back to the office later.

31
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:32,430
You do know "Infernal Affairs" has three films, right?

32
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:35,430
Are you planning to leave before we finish them?

33
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:38,640
I have to watch all three before I can go?

34
00:01:40,870 --> 00:01:42,710
Then I'll have to cancel today's meetings.

35
00:01:44,510 --> 00:01:46,710
You're really staying to keep me company today?

36
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:49,640
Really.

37
00:01:51,230 --> 00:01:56,040
Since I'm cancelling the meetings and we have all this time,

38
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,790
there's no need to rush through the films.

39
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:08,860
[Infernal Affairs]

40
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,740
♪With you, it's like I can breathe again♪

41
00:02:42,170 --> 00:02:44,940
♪I can't live without this breath, this heartbeat♪

42
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:47,850
♪Forever's too far, but you're right here♪

43
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:50,280
♪Together we'll take on this jaded world♪

44
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:53,260
♪With you, I'll cross the dark, outrun the pain, and run away♪

45
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:57,420
♪Still believing in true love, no matter how naive, calling you♪

46
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,210
♪I'm willing to wait♪

47
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:05,900
♪I love you like you're a part of me♪

48
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:08,700
♪I want to share my life with you♪

49
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:15,120
♪To love this deeply, I'll give a little more♪

50
00:03:15,470 --> 00:03:17,270
♪In this cold and gray city♪

51
00:03:17,350 --> 00:03:18,980
♪Through all the pain, I'll hold you. Is it true?♪

52
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:21,430
♪Pieces of our memories slowly fade♪

53
00:03:21,510 --> 00:03:22,090
♪Stay with me♪

54
00:03:22,230 --> 00:03:24,840
♪Do you remember the day we crossed paths?♪

55
00:03:24,920 --> 00:03:25,620
♪Stay with me♪

56
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:28,540
♪Do you remember the forever we promised?♪

57
00:03:29,030 --> 00:03:31,040
♪Who's waiting for you to save them?♪

58
00:03:31,570 --> 00:03:34,080
♪My heart aches, breaks, and struggles on♪

59
00:03:34,610 --> 00:03:37,120
♪How can I hold on to everything in one moment?♪

60
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:41,340
♪Stop blaming fate and learn to let it be♪

61
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:45,220
[Ash]
[Episode 8]

62
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:48,960
I brought Dreamweaver in to deal with my second uncle and my father

63
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,150
because I didn't want to become the leader

64
00:03:51,150 --> 00:03:52,710
only to be controlled by others at every turn.

65
00:03:53,310 --> 00:03:54,310
If that's the case,

66
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,590
I'd rather go to war with them directly.

67
00:03:55,710 --> 00:03:56,750
Going to war isn't a problem.

68
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,400
But if we're really going to fight,

69
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:00,520
we need to take out their leader directly.

70
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,910
So you asked me here for a face-to-face handover

71
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:04,280
because you wanted to force my hand.

72
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:11,030
Ms. Ho,

73
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:12,560
it's been a pleasure knowing you.

74
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:13,310
Shawn,

75
00:04:13,470 --> 00:04:14,960
Eastern Hall has considerable influence.

76
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:16,950
I'm sure there are still ways we can help Dreamweaver.

77
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,630
Spare Ms. Ho.

78
00:04:18,630 --> 00:04:20,000
I can spare her,

79
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:21,360
but I have one condition.

80
00:04:21,390 --> 00:04:22,000
You

81
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:23,830
have to come with me.

82
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:26,000
Foon Gor,

83
00:04:26,430 --> 00:04:27,870
bear with this for a bit.

84
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,270
Welcome.

85
00:04:37,870 --> 00:04:38,680
Sorry.

86
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:40,120
I put you through a lot.

87
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:41,870
Are you feeling okay?

88
00:04:44,630 --> 00:04:45,720
Where am I?

89
00:04:45,950 --> 00:04:46,920
My place.

90
00:04:47,510 --> 00:04:48,310
Well?

91
00:04:49,070 --> 00:04:49,950
What do you think of it?

92
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:52,070
It's nice.

93
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:53,920
Looks pretty comfortable.

94
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:55,920
I'm glad you like it.

95
00:04:56,830 --> 00:04:57,630
Foon Gor,

96
00:04:58,270 --> 00:05:00,040
now you can finally stay by my side.

97
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:03,240
Stay by your side?

98
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:07,070
Yes. Actually, I've always wanted

99
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,270
to be with you.

100
00:05:10,870 --> 00:05:11,750
Be with me?

101
00:05:13,590 --> 00:05:14,820
So since we were kids, you've been...

102
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:15,110
That's right.

103
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:17,920
Do you remember?

104
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:19,510
When I was little,

105
00:05:20,430 --> 00:05:23,630
my mum and I were beaten by that awful father of mine every day.

106
00:05:23,830 --> 00:05:24,870
I was always injured

107
00:05:25,510 --> 00:05:26,720
here or there.

108
00:05:27,830 --> 00:05:28,720
What did my mum do?

109
00:05:29,270 --> 00:05:31,430
She didn't even dare say a word for me.

110
00:05:31,870 --> 00:05:33,560
She thought that was how she could protect me.

111
00:05:34,430 --> 00:05:35,680
But it didn't matter

112
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,560
because I had you.

113
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:39,430
Without you,

114
00:05:39,870 --> 00:05:41,510
he might've beaten me to death.

115
00:05:42,070 --> 00:05:44,160
I might not even be alive today.

116
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:54,040
Shawn,

117
00:05:54,630 --> 00:05:57,430
I know it was the lack of care

118
00:05:57,430 --> 00:05:59,560
from your family that made you

119
00:06:00,070 --> 00:06:01,560
remember even the littlest things

120
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:02,750
I did for you.

121
00:06:02,950 --> 00:06:04,270
They weren't little things.

122
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,560
That day,

123
00:06:06,830 --> 00:06:10,480
for the first time in my life, someone said he'd protect me

124
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:12,070
and stay with me through the hard times.

125
00:06:12,270 --> 00:06:13,120
It was the first time

126
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:15,830
I had felt like someone actually saw me.

127
00:06:16,630 --> 00:06:19,040
It was like I was trapped in a pitch-black room,

128
00:06:19,270 --> 00:06:20,830
and someone turned on a light for me.

129
00:06:21,310 --> 00:06:24,040
It made me feel like my life still had possibilities,

130
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,560
like things could still change.

131
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,480
And that someone was you.

132
00:06:30,070 --> 00:06:31,830
You survived in the UK

133
00:06:32,630 --> 00:06:34,480
and achieved everything you have now

134
00:06:34,630 --> 00:06:36,310
because of yourself.

135
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:39,560
I just happened to be there at the time.

136
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:41,430
I'm not as important as you make me out to be.

137
00:06:42,070 --> 00:06:44,240
No, that's not true.

138
00:06:46,070 --> 00:06:47,480
After you moved away,

139
00:06:48,430 --> 00:06:50,240
everything changed.

140
00:06:54,270 --> 00:06:55,800
Enough! Stop hitting him!

141
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:57,160
You'll end up killing him!

142
00:06:58,870 --> 00:07:01,270
I'm hitting him because he's my son!

143
00:07:01,270 --> 00:07:02,830
You're really asking for it!

144
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,870
That day, he beat us again.

145
00:07:07,270 --> 00:07:09,340
My mum didn't dare to fight back.

146
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:11,800
Do you think I'm useless?

147
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,190
Help!

148
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:15,870
She thought if we just endured it, we'd get through it.

149
00:07:18,260 --> 00:07:21,830
But I ended up watching her die right in front of me.

150
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:24,580
It wasn't my fault.

151
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:26,020
It really wasn't my fault!

152
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:26,830
He was vicious.

153
00:07:27,430 --> 00:07:29,950
He said if I told anyone,

154
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:33,160
he'd beat me to death too.

155
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:34,830
What do you want?

156
00:07:35,270 --> 00:07:37,270
But I could tell

157
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:39,160
he was terrified.

158
00:07:40,630 --> 00:07:43,630
I'd never seen him that scared before.

159
00:07:45,190 --> 00:07:46,360
It really wasn't my fault!

160
00:07:46,940 --> 00:07:48,100
Turns out he's scared too.

161
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:50,620
Suddenly, I wasn't afraid of anything anymore.

162
00:07:52,310 --> 00:07:54,270
Either way, I could die,

163
00:07:54,630 --> 00:07:57,630
and I wasn't going to die like she did.

164
00:08:14,190 --> 00:08:16,000
Even when you weren't by my side, Foon Gor,

165
00:08:16,950 --> 00:08:19,360
I never forgot what you told me.

166
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,190
So I killed him.

167
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:24,680
That day,

168
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:27,190
I took everything valuable from the house

169
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:29,480
and went to an uncle in a Chinatown in London.

170
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:31,950
who was involved with a Chinese gang.

171
00:08:32,550 --> 00:08:34,000
I never returned to Hong Kong, China,

172
00:08:35,030 --> 00:08:37,080
or told anyone what happened.

173
00:08:37,630 --> 00:08:40,790
When I finally founded Feros and Dreamweaver,

174
00:08:41,790 --> 00:08:45,200
I knew I was finally in a position to come back.

175
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,790
So when you told me

176
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,440
you'd been adopted by a British couple,

177
00:08:52,270 --> 00:08:53,840
lost touch with your parents,

178
00:08:54,270 --> 00:08:55,630
and never saw them again,

179
00:08:55,630 --> 00:08:56,870
that was all a lie?

180
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:59,550
I'm the head of a listed company, after all.

181
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,630
I have an image to maintain.

182
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:05,080
But after I came back,

183
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:07,840
I found out you were involved with Hui Loek To.

184
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:11,000
I spent a long time

185
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,670
thinking about one question:

186
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:15,360
why would you be with someone like him?

187
00:09:15,870 --> 00:09:17,550
Didn't I meet you first?

188
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:19,790
Wasn't I your first friend?

189
00:09:19,870 --> 00:09:21,270
Wasn't I the first person you protected

190
00:09:21,550 --> 00:09:23,000
and truly cared about?

191
00:09:25,790 --> 00:09:27,080
Was it just because he was rich

192
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:28,550
and had a privileged upbringing?

193
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,360
Was it just because being with him

194
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,550
meant you could have a better life?

195
00:09:33,270 --> 00:09:34,840
I get it, actually.

196
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,360
For people like us who grew up in public housing,

197
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,790
if we want a better life,

198
00:09:42,150 --> 00:09:44,270
the only way

199
00:09:44,270 --> 00:09:46,000
is to befriend rich people like him.

200
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:48,630
You did the right thing.

201
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:55,960
But things are different now.

202
00:09:56,550 --> 00:09:58,200
I'm not the Siu Yan I used to be.

203
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:01,200
Now I'm just as rich and powerful

204
00:10:01,270 --> 00:10:02,790
as Hui Loek To.

205
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,360
I have just as much money

206
00:10:06,030 --> 00:10:08,550
and power as he does, if not more.

207
00:10:09,390 --> 00:10:12,360
I have more than enough money for us

208
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:14,480
to live comfortably for the rest of our lives.

209
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,360
No one will ever bully you again.

210
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:18,200
You won't have to answer to anyone

211
00:10:18,550 --> 00:10:20,870
or put up with Hui Loek To anymore.

212
00:10:22,030 --> 00:10:23,910
Hui Loek To doesn't deserve to be by your side.

213
00:10:23,910 --> 00:10:25,750
He can't even protect you properly.

214
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:26,840
No need to wait.

215
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:28,390
Chairman Yiu won't be able to make it today.

216
00:10:28,510 --> 00:10:29,320
My surname is Siu.

217
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:31,670
I'm the CEO of Feros Group.

218
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:34,120
If you need to work with Feros,

219
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:35,390
come talk to me anytime.

220
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:36,630
I look forward to it.

221
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:38,600
I went after Tin Ping

222
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:40,900
and used To Si Hong to circulate the notes through Sheng Tung.

223
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:42,510
No matter how good they are,

224
00:10:42,670 --> 00:10:43,840
they're still counterfeit notes.

225
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,200
Using so many at once

226
00:10:45,510 --> 00:10:46,390
is bound to draw attention.

227
00:10:46,390 --> 00:10:47,960
I don't know what Dreamweaver is.

228
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,270
The currency counterfeiting syndicate!

229
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:50,960
Do you think I'm a fool?

230
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:52,200
Fei Foon...

231
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,000
Don't call me Fei Foon.

232
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:53,670
Call me Officer!

233
00:10:58,550 --> 00:11:00,000
Then I sent Mr. Wong over to stir things up.

234
00:11:00,030 --> 00:11:02,240
I wanted to run Hui Loek To in circles

235
00:11:02,510 --> 00:11:04,720
and leave him unable to explain himself to you.

236
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:06,630
He paints himself as an honest businessman,

237
00:11:06,630 --> 00:11:08,270
but he's really a gangster!

238
00:11:09,630 --> 00:11:10,630
But once he got to the station,

239
00:11:10,630 --> 00:11:11,510
he wouldn't say a word

240
00:11:11,510 --> 00:11:12,390
or get a lawyer.

241
00:11:12,630 --> 00:11:13,910
He refuses to talk unless the media are around,

242
00:11:14,270 --> 00:11:15,630
like we're the ones out to get him.

243
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:17,510
What exactly is he trying to do?

244
00:11:17,550 --> 00:11:18,910
Is he only after media attention?

245
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:21,720
Who knows? Either way, he's a real headache.

246
00:11:22,870 --> 00:11:25,080
Someone as proud as you

247
00:11:25,150 --> 00:11:27,840
shouldn't have to put yourself beneath someone like Hui Loek To.

248
00:11:29,670 --> 00:11:31,630
You won't have to risk your life anymore.

249
00:11:33,270 --> 00:11:34,440
From now on,

250
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:35,870
stay by my side.

251
00:11:36,870 --> 00:11:38,440
Let's build a life together.

252
00:11:38,670 --> 00:11:39,550
Okay?

253
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,030
Whatever you want,

254
00:11:41,750 --> 00:11:43,120
I'll give it to you.

255
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:45,320
And I'll always protect you.

256
00:11:46,670 --> 00:11:47,670
I'll give you

257
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,440
anything you want

258
00:11:49,670 --> 00:11:51,440
and keep you from harm.

259
00:11:53,870 --> 00:11:54,960
Thank you, Shawn.

260
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:58,750
I'm a little tired right now.

261
00:11:59,670 --> 00:12:03,440
Can you give me some time and space?

262
00:12:03,750 --> 00:12:04,670
Of course.

263
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,840
As much as you need.

264
00:12:17,910 --> 00:12:19,440
This whole room is yours.

265
00:12:19,910 --> 00:12:21,910
Stay as long as you like.

266
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:24,840
If you need anything, just call the men outside.

267
00:12:25,150 --> 00:12:27,910
They'll be outside the door 24 hours a day to protect you.

268
00:12:28,910 --> 00:12:31,150
Okay. Thanks.

269
00:12:31,150 --> 00:12:31,960
No problem.

270
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:34,670
Get some rest.

271
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,030
How did it go?

272
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:15,910
I went in with the lawyer.

273
00:13:17,030 --> 00:13:18,270
The police said

274
00:13:18,670 --> 00:13:19,720
that in yesterday's shooting,

275
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:21,670
none of those arrested,

276
00:13:22,270 --> 00:13:23,630
killed, or injured

277
00:13:24,030 --> 00:13:27,270
was named Mok Fei Foon.

278
00:13:28,270 --> 00:13:29,440
None? How is that possible?

279
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:32,960
He spoke to me last night

280
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:34,480
and said he'd definitely be here tonight.

281
00:13:35,630 --> 00:13:37,080
So why can't anyone find him now?

282
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:43,270
Could he have run away

283
00:13:43,550 --> 00:13:44,630
like he did last time?

284
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:50,510
Hi, I can't take your call right now...

285
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:52,670
He's still not picking up.

286
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:54,670
Calm down.

287
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:56,630
Look on the bright side.

288
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:59,150
None of the casualties named by the police

289
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,360
was Mok Fei Foon.

290
00:14:00,870 --> 00:14:02,440
Doesn't that mean he's okay?

291
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:03,870
Try not to worry so much.

292
00:14:04,030 --> 00:14:05,480
How can I not worry?

293
00:14:06,670 --> 00:14:08,150
If he's really okay,

294
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:09,240
why can't anyone find him

295
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:10,240
or get through to him?

296
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:12,270
Am I supposed to act as if nothing happened?

297
00:14:19,510 --> 00:14:21,910
He was perfectly fine. How did he suddenly go missing?

298
00:14:27,270 --> 00:14:28,670
I really can't answer that.

299
00:14:30,270 --> 00:14:32,080
Should we ask someone who knows

300
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:32,960
what's going on?

301
00:14:37,670 --> 00:14:38,670
Wait here for me.

302
00:15:02,510 --> 00:15:03,320
Officer Chan.

303
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:06,270
Mr. Hui?

304
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,270
How can I help you?

305
00:15:09,030 --> 00:15:11,270
Tell me if Fei Foon is okay.

306
00:15:12,030 --> 00:15:13,080
Why are you asking me that?

307
00:15:13,510 --> 00:15:14,550
And why come to me?

308
00:15:15,270 --> 00:15:16,550
How much do you know?

309
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:18,480
I'm his boyfriend.

310
00:15:18,630 --> 00:15:19,720
I know everything about him.

311
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:22,870
I don't know much about his undercover work,

312
00:15:23,750 --> 00:15:25,630
but I know you're his handler.

313
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:27,270
He's on the counterfeit money case,

314
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:29,440
and I'm worried about his safety.

315
00:15:29,910 --> 00:15:31,240
Is that enough of an answer?

316
00:15:32,670 --> 00:15:33,550
Boyfriend?

317
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:39,720
So you know about everything he's doing?

318
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:41,270
But do you realise

319
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:42,720
that if you expose his identity,

320
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:43,510
you could get him killed?

321
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:46,270
I'm not interested in internal police matters.

322
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:48,870
If I really knew everything,

323
00:15:48,870 --> 00:15:50,440
I wouldn't need to go to all this trouble,

324
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:51,480
waiting here for you

325
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:52,510
just to ask where he is.

326
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:56,510
I only want to know one thing:

327
00:15:56,870 --> 00:15:57,840
is he safe?

328
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:59,670
Just give me a straight answer, and I'll leave.

329
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:01,630
Then I'll be honest with you.

330
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:03,630
I don't know where he is either.

331
00:16:04,270 --> 00:16:05,080
What?

332
00:16:05,670 --> 00:16:07,030
You don't know where he is?

333
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:09,320
What kind of superior are you?

334
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:10,120
I didn't want this to happen either.

335
00:16:11,670 --> 00:16:12,750
A case this big

336
00:16:12,750 --> 00:16:13,960
is something I've only seen a handful of times

337
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:15,080
in all my years as a cop.

338
00:16:16,550 --> 00:16:17,870
Fei Foon was the one who told me

339
00:16:17,870 --> 00:16:19,510
he was confident he could handle it.

340
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:22,630
I can't tell you any more details.

341
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:25,670
But if you know anything, tell me.

342
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:27,960
Who else has he been in contact with

343
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:28,870
besides you?

344
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:29,510
If that's the case,

345
00:16:29,510 --> 00:16:30,630
I have nothing to say to you.

346
00:16:30,630 --> 00:16:31,150
Don't leave,

347
00:16:31,150 --> 00:16:32,480
or I'll charge you with obstructing the police.

348
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:35,030
Are you threatening me?

349
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:37,440
If you don't want to put Fei Foon in danger,

350
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:38,870
then tell me everything you know.

351
00:16:39,030 --> 00:16:39,870
Don't try anything funny!

352
00:16:39,870 --> 00:16:40,720
What did you say?

353
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:41,550
Let go.

354
00:16:41,550 --> 00:16:42,670
You think I'm putting Fei Foon in danger?

355
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:44,240
You're the one who sent him on a mission

356
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:45,080
where he could easily get killed

357
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:46,270
and failed to protect him.

358
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:47,870
I won't go easy on you because of Fei Foon.

359
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,720
I really will charge you with assaulting a police officer.

360
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:51,270
Let go.

361
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:56,910
If you've got so much time,

362
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:59,360
spend it finding out where he is.

363
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:00,360
Spend more time

364
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:01,670
protecting your own officers!

365
00:17:02,670 --> 00:17:04,270
If anything really happens to him,

366
00:17:04,550 --> 00:17:06,310
can you give him his life back?

367
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:10,960
Stop.

368
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:12,110
What now?

369
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:13,510
Take out your phone.

370
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:17,880
I'll give you my number.

371
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:19,720
I want to find him too.

372
00:17:21,110 --> 00:17:22,880
If either of us hears anything, let the other know.

373
00:17:37,350 --> 00:17:38,550
How many men does Sheng Tung have?

374
00:17:39,270 --> 00:17:40,440
Free or not,

375
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:41,750
send every one of them out.

376
00:17:41,750 --> 00:17:43,270
We have to find Fei Foon.

377
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,270
Understood.

378
00:17:58,030 --> 00:17:59,240
Morning, Foon Gor.

379
00:17:59,750 --> 00:18:00,550
Morning, Shawn.

380
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:02,680
You look much better now.

381
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:03,720
Yeah.

382
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:05,680
It's pretty comfortable here.

383
00:18:05,830 --> 00:18:07,110
I slept well last night too.

384
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:08,550
Good.

385
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,880
Have you thought

386
00:18:12,510 --> 00:18:13,880
about what I said yesterday?

387
00:18:14,070 --> 00:18:15,750
I have.

388
00:18:16,070 --> 00:18:18,880
Why don't we go out today?

389
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:21,110
I'd like to get to know you better.

390
00:18:21,270 --> 00:18:22,030
Really?

391
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:23,510
Sure.

392
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:25,590
I wasn't prepared

393
00:18:25,590 --> 00:18:26,640
for you to say that at all.

394
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:28,110
I'd better go change.

395
00:18:29,030 --> 00:18:30,750
I'll have my men get a car ready.

396
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:32,510
It's our first time going out together,

397
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:33,960
so we should dress to match.

398
00:18:37,350 --> 00:18:38,480
Foon Gor, check out these jackets.

399
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:54,070
This one looks like it'd suit you.

400
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:56,110
Foon Gor, wear this one.

401
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:57,440
Sure.

402
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:58,960
I'll go change.

403
00:18:59,070 --> 00:19:00,030
Wait here for me.

404
00:19:00,270 --> 00:19:01,160
I won't be long.

405
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:03,240
Take your time.

406
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:14,040
[Danger]

407
00:19:14,070 --> 00:19:15,750
I've been back in Hong Kong, China for a while,

408
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:18,920
but this is my first time coming here for some fresh air.

409
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:20,510
Really?

410
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:23,880
So you've never been here before?

411
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:26,240
No.

412
00:19:28,030 --> 00:19:30,030
I've seen it plenty of times on TV,

413
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:33,030
but I never realised until now

414
00:19:33,750 --> 00:19:35,270
how beautiful it really is.

415
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:37,550
And I get to come here with you.

416
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:39,440
It's nice.

417
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:42,720
Is that so?

418
00:19:44,750 --> 00:19:46,750
Then we should do something to remember this.

419
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:49,480
Like what?

420
00:20:00,270 --> 00:20:01,440
Do you have a knife?

421
00:20:09,030 --> 00:20:10,480
What should I draw?

422
00:20:13,110 --> 00:20:14,270
I've got an idea.

423
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:38,750
What's that?

424
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,030
A pineapple bun.

425
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:42,510
To remember the first time we met.

426
00:20:43,510 --> 00:20:45,510
You're so sweet, Foon Gor.

427
00:20:46,270 --> 00:20:48,750
Talking about it is making me hungry.

428
00:20:49,030 --> 00:20:50,510
Let's go to that restaurant and get something to eat.

429
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:52,680
Sure. I'm getting hungry too.

430
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:12,030
Foon Gor,

431
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:14,350
is this still your favourite restaurant?

432
00:21:14,830 --> 00:21:15,640
Yeah.

433
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:17,830
I've been coming here since I was little.

434
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:19,880
I've grown attached to this place.

435
00:21:21,550 --> 00:21:22,350
Sir.

436
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:23,880
Coming. Just a moment.

437
00:21:27,750 --> 00:21:29,070
Haven't seen you in a while.

438
00:21:29,110 --> 00:21:30,270
What would you like?

439
00:21:32,070 --> 00:21:32,880
Sir.

440
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:33,160
Yes?

441
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:35,510
Two pineapple buns with butter.

442
00:21:35,510 --> 00:21:36,030
Sure.

443
00:21:36,030 --> 00:21:36,830
Wait.

444
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:42,160
I feel like having something different today.

445
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:42,960
Sure.

446
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:48,110
One satay beef noodles from the Afternoon Tea section.

447
00:21:48,270 --> 00:21:51,830
And one BBQ pork spaghetti in soup.

448
00:21:51,830 --> 00:21:52,440
Sure.

449
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:53,480
What do you want to drink?

450
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:55,440
Anything's fine.

451
00:21:55,550 --> 00:21:57,270
Two iced lemon teas with less ice.

452
00:21:57,350 --> 00:21:58,160
Okay.

453
00:21:59,440 --> 00:22:00,270
Coming right up.

454
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:03,480
Foon Gor.

455
00:22:03,830 --> 00:22:06,110
Don't you usually order a buttered pineapple bun?

456
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:07,680
Why aren't you having one today?

457
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:12,030
Sometimes I feel like trying something different.

458
00:22:13,110 --> 00:22:15,440
More importantly, we need to finish quickly

459
00:22:15,440 --> 00:22:16,830
so we can catch the 5:10 film.

460
00:22:16,830 --> 00:22:17,640
What do you say?

461
00:22:17,750 --> 00:22:18,550
Sure.

462
00:22:46,270 --> 00:22:47,440
I need to use the restroom.

463
00:22:47,510 --> 00:22:49,160
You keep watching. I'll be right back.

464
00:22:50,110 --> 00:22:50,920
Okay.

465
00:23:11,110 --> 00:23:12,640
Mr. Mok, where are you going?

466
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:18,270
Foon Gor, where are you going?

467
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:23,240
Shawn,

468
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:24,920
why don't you just turn yourself in?

469
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:27,880
Turn myself in? Why?

470
00:23:28,070 --> 00:23:30,440
You make counterfeit money, and you killed people at Eastern Hall.

471
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:31,920
This has gone too far.

472
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:35,350
So you never intended to be with me, did you?

473
00:23:35,350 --> 00:23:36,160
That's right.

474
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:38,160
I know what happened when you were little

475
00:23:38,160 --> 00:23:39,270
is what made you who you are today.

476
00:23:39,640 --> 00:23:41,240
But you're not a bad person at heart.

477
00:23:42,030 --> 00:23:43,270
Come with me and turn yourself in.

478
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:45,550
I'll ask the judge to show you leniency.

479
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:48,350
I see.

480
00:23:50,960 --> 00:23:53,830
I thought you were different from everyone else.

481
00:23:54,440 --> 00:23:55,720
I thought you understood me

482
00:23:55,720 --> 00:23:56,830
and genuinely wanted to be my friend.

483
00:23:57,510 --> 00:24:02,160
But from the moment you said you wanted to know about Dreamweaver

484
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:04,640
to going out with me today,

485
00:24:05,750 --> 00:24:07,240
it was all just so you could arrest me.

486
00:24:12,440 --> 00:24:13,550
But that's okay.

487
00:24:15,310 --> 00:24:17,720
I know you've just got stuck in your own head.

488
00:24:17,960 --> 00:24:18,750
Don't worry.

489
00:24:18,750 --> 00:24:19,720
I'm not angry with you.

490
00:24:20,270 --> 00:24:21,550
We have plenty of time.

491
00:24:22,110 --> 00:24:23,510
You'll understand me eventually.

492
00:24:23,510 --> 00:24:24,240
I won't.

493
00:24:24,240 --> 00:24:25,110
Trust me. You will.

494
00:24:25,110 --> 00:24:26,510
Shawn, let go of me.

495
00:24:27,790 --> 00:24:29,590
It's not too late to turn back now.

496
00:24:30,350 --> 00:24:31,750
The police will find you soon.

497
00:24:31,750 --> 00:24:32,750
You won't get away.

498
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:34,440
Boys,

499
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:35,880
let's go home first.

500
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:36,880
Hey, what are you doing?

501
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:39,440
Shawn, it's still not too late to turn back!

502
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:40,270
Be good.

503
00:24:41,070 --> 00:24:42,440
We'll talk later.

504
00:24:52,680 --> 00:24:53,480
Come in.

505
00:25:16,240 --> 00:25:17,030
Wait.

506
00:25:17,750 --> 00:25:19,310
Cancel all my meetings today.

507
00:25:19,680 --> 00:25:20,440
Okay.

508
00:25:31,310 --> 00:25:32,440
Any news?

509
00:25:35,960 --> 00:25:36,920
Keep looking.

510
00:26:04,880 --> 00:26:05,880
Wait for me.

511
00:27:35,880 --> 00:27:36,720
Foon Gor.

512
00:27:37,070 --> 00:27:38,270
What's wrong?

513
00:27:38,550 --> 00:27:40,200
Are you feeling okay?

514
00:27:40,480 --> 00:27:42,000
Let me help you lie down.

515
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:44,920
Where am I?

516
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:46,310
You're safe here.

517
00:27:46,960 --> 00:27:48,240
We're home.

518
00:27:49,110 --> 00:27:51,310
Just get some rest, okay?

519
00:27:52,200 --> 00:27:53,510
I'll take good care of you.

520
00:27:58,030 --> 00:27:58,830
Hui... Hui Loek To...

521
00:28:03,750 --> 00:28:04,310
Don't worry.

522
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:06,550
No one here can hurt you.

523
00:28:07,310 --> 00:28:08,680
Not even Hui Loek To.

524
00:28:24,880 --> 00:28:26,030
Bring him back.

525
00:28:36,750 --> 00:28:37,640
Give me the syringe.

526
00:28:52,660 --> 00:28:55,830
[Danger]

527
00:28:55,840 --> 00:28:57,550
What's gotten into you, coming to keep me company?

528
00:28:58,240 --> 00:29:00,680
No reason. Can't I just spend time with you?

529
00:29:02,480 --> 00:29:03,440
Don't worry.

530
00:29:04,880 --> 00:29:06,270
Until I find Fei Foon,

531
00:29:06,550 --> 00:29:07,750
I'm not going to die.

532
00:29:08,920 --> 00:29:09,750
I know.

533
00:29:11,030 --> 00:29:13,270
But if...

534
00:29:14,030 --> 00:29:15,240
I'm only saying if.

535
00:29:15,510 --> 00:29:17,440
If you find out he's really dead,

536
00:29:17,680 --> 00:29:19,030
what are you going to do?

537
00:29:22,550 --> 00:29:23,350
Get revenge.

538
00:29:26,830 --> 00:29:29,440
I'll make whoever killed him pay.

539
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:31,640
No matter what it takes,

540
00:29:31,880 --> 00:29:33,680
I'll keep going until my last breath.

541
00:29:33,680 --> 00:29:34,640
And when my time comes,

542
00:29:34,640 --> 00:29:35,640
I'll finally see him again.

543
00:30:02,270 --> 00:30:04,400
What's so special about this bin?

544
00:30:20,640 --> 00:30:22,960
Hey, I haven't got in yet!

545
00:30:29,750 --> 00:30:30,830
Sir.

546
00:30:30,830 --> 00:30:31,640
Excuse me.

547
00:30:33,160 --> 00:30:35,000
Have you seen this man?

548
00:30:37,160 --> 00:30:38,590
He's a regular.

549
00:30:38,590 --> 00:30:39,720
He was just here.

550
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:41,200
Did he leave any message?

551
00:30:41,200 --> 00:30:42,640
I really need to find him.

552
00:30:43,110 --> 00:30:43,920
I don't think so.

553
00:30:44,160 --> 00:30:45,400
Think carefully.

554
00:30:48,200 --> 00:30:48,960
No, he didn't.

555
00:30:49,350 --> 00:30:51,400
But he was acting a bit strangely.

556
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:52,200
All these years,

557
00:30:52,240 --> 00:30:54,310
he's always ordered milk tea, fish balls, and buttered pineapple buns.

558
00:30:54,350 --> 00:30:58,200
That day, he switched to satay beef noodles and BBQ pork spaghetti in soup.

559
00:31:00,830 --> 00:31:02,160
Do you have a menu?

560
00:31:02,350 --> 00:31:03,510
Yes. Just a moment.

561
00:31:07,160 --> 00:31:07,960
